    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <algorithm>\\n#include <climits>\\n\\n// Fast integer reading using getchar_unlocked (thread-unsafe but fast)\\nstatic inline int read_int() {\\n    int x = 0;\\n    char c = getchar_unlocked();\\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar_unlocked(); // skip whitespace\\n    bool neg = false;\\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar_unlocked(); }\\n    do {\\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\\n        c = getchar_unlocked();\\n    } while (c > ' ');\\n    return neg ? -x : x;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n = read_int();\\n    int s = read_int();\\n\\n    // Read entire matrix into a flat array for cache locality and later parallel processing\\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n            mat[i * n + j] = read_int();\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Integral image: pref[i][j] = sum of submatrix from (0,0) to (i-1,j-1)\\n    const int np1 = n + 1;\\n    std::vector<long long> pref(np1 * np1, 0LL);\\n\\n    // First pass: row-wise cumulative sums (parallel over rows)\\n#pragma omp parallel for\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n        long long sum = 0;\\n        int base_row = i * n;\\n        int pref_row = (i + 1) * np1;\\n#pragma ivdep\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\\n            sum += mat[base_row + j];\\n            pref[pref_row + j + 1] = sum;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Second pass: vertical accumulation (parallel over columns)\\n#pragma omp parallel for\\n    for (int j = 0; j <= n; ++j) {\\n        long long cum = 0;\\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\\n            pref[i * np1 + j] += pref[(i - 1) * np1 + j];\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using blocking to improve cache reuse\\n    const int B = 64;\\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\\n\\n    for (int ii = 0; ii < n - s + 1; ii += B) {\\n        int i_end = std::min(ii + B, n - s + 1);\\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < n - s + 1; jj += B) {\\n            int j_end = std::min(jj + B, n - s + 1);\\n#pragma ivdep\\n            for (int i = ii; i < i_end; ++i) {\\n                const long long * __restrict__ row_i_s = &pref[(i + s) * np1];\\n                const long long * __restrict__ row_i   = &pref[i * np1];\\n#pragma ivdep\\n                for (int j = jj; j < j_end; ++j) {\\n                    long long sum = row_i_s[j + s] - row_i[j + s]\\n                                   - row_i_s[j] + row_i[j];\\n                    if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Integrating fast integer input (source A), flattened matrix storage for cache locality (source B), OpenMP-parallelized integral image construction via two passes (sources B/C), and cache-blocked search with vectorization hints (source A) yields a correct, high-performance solution that outperforms any single-source variant on the target ARM64 platform.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Input is read sequentially using getchar_unlocked before parallel prefix computation to ensure thread safety. The integral image uses two passes: row-wise cumulative sums then vertical accumulation, both parallelized with OpenMP. Search phase employs loop tiling (block size 64) and restrict/ivdep pragmas for auto-vectorization. All intermediate computations use long long; final result is cast to int as required by the problem statement.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [\n    \"501b40ba23ab496f\",\n    \"015bd08c24cf4419\",\n    \"8e2ef19488ab48a4\"\n  ],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Use custom fast integer reader (getchar_unlocked) from source A\",\n    \"Replace vector<vector<int>> with flat contiguous vector<int> for better cache locality and SIMD access patterns (source B)\",